abstract: >-
  Determines the space of rational alternating forms invariant under the
  (3,4,∞) matrices T1, T2 in Alpöge's self-hosted note. That space is
  one-dimensional, generated by an explicit integral matrix Ω0 of type
  (1,6). A functorial symplectic 2-form (tether fragment) on this lattice
  is necessarily a scalar multiple of ω0. Does not prove a compactification
  theorem. Lean 4 library OmegaZero34 is the kernel-checked form of the
  lattice theorems. Author: Benjamin Stanley Frohman.
